  "construction": "Reversing fold of a pair-partition CPM CSS code of arXiv:2609.30069 with J = 4, L = 10, P = 18. Parent qubit q = c*P + t. Parent X row (j,s) meets c*P + ((s - E[j][c]) mod P) for each block c. The involution is pi(c*P + t) = sigma[c]*P + ((-t - B[sigma[c]]) mod P). Folded site i pairs the i-th smallest q with q < pi(q) with pi(q). Each parent X row becomes one generator, X where it meets a representative and Z where it meets a partner. E = [[5, 3, 14, 12, 8, 6, 2, 15, 10, 2], [13, 2, 12, 5, 3, 0, 2, 4, 12, 12], [14, 9, 3, 17, 16, 8, 0, 1, 11, 14], [7, 0, 3, 7, 11, 0, 7, 7, 16, 11]], sigma = [5, 8, 6, 7, 9, 0, 2, 3, 1, 4], B = [3, 14, 13, 14, 17, 3, 13, 14, 14, 17].",
  "references": [
   "arXiv:2609.30069",
   "https://github.com/ultra-high-rate-qec/design-principles-data"
  ],
  "date": "2026",
